From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:31:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Never revoke a certificate, and create one only when the
 account has none
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the account's certificates had no private key on the device, the
sign-in flow offered to revoke them (for a free team, "Revoke" was the
main button) or created one more. A certificate the account already has
signs every app installed with it, from the computer or from another
SideStore: revoking it stops them all from opening.

The flow now creates a certificate only when the account has none at
all, whatever their names, since the one a computer made (iloader's, for
instance) may not be named "iOS Development". Otherwise it stops with an
error that asks the user to import the certificate from the SideStore
that uses it, then to retry; the Retry, Skip and Cancel choices are the
ones every provisioning error already offers. Revoking or creating one
stays possible by hand in Settings → Advanced Settings → Certificate
Management.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJorvBGmBB88WUcRVhE7
